    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The activation of mTORC1 is initiated by the Rag GTPase complex, specifically RagA and RagB, which are stimulated by leucine binding to its receptor complex. When leucine levels are high, it triggers the dimerization and activation of RagA and RagB, which then interact with the mTORC1 Complex to initiate a signaling cascade. \n\nThe Rag-GTR (Adaptor) protein, Guanine Triphosphate Release complex, senses high leucine levels by interacting with the leucine receptor, ultimately releasing GTP and triggering Rag GTPase dimerization. As the Rag GTPase dimer comes into proximity with the mTOR to cuboid protein recycling,  linker fusion results; forming an: activating complex ( RagTOR signaling module).",
